{"id":129,"verdict":"keep","top1":"The dog ate it","textAnswers":[{"rank":1,"texts":["The dog ate it","My dog ate it","The dog ate my homework"]},{"rank":2,"texts":["I forgot","I forgot about it","I forgot we had homework"]},{"rank":3,"texts":["I left it at home","I left it home","Left it at home"]},{"rank":4,"texts":["I lost it","I lost my homework","I can't find it"]},{"rank":5,"texts":["I was sick","I was ill","I felt sick"]},{"rank":6,"texts":["I didn't understand it","I didn't get it","It was too hard"]},{"rank":7,"texts":["My printer broke","The printer broke","Printer ran out of ink"]},{"rank":8,"texts":["I didn't have time","I ran out of time","No time"]},{"rank":9,"texts":["My computer crashed","My laptop died","Computer broke"]},{"rank":10,"texts":["I was too busy","I had too much other homework","Too much homework"]},{"rank":11,"texts":["I left it at school","Left it in my locker","Left it at school"]},{"rank":12,"texts":["My little brother ruined it","My sister ruined it","My brother drew on it"]},{"rank":13,"texts":["The Wi-Fi was down","No internet","Internet went out"]},{"rank":14,"texts":["I ran out of ink","My pen ran out","Pen died"]},{"rank":15,"texts":["My bag got wet","It got wet","It rained on it"]},{"rank":16,"texts":["I had practice","I had soccer practice","I had a game"]},{"rank":17,"texts":["I fell asleep","I fell asleep doing it"]},{"rank":18,"texts":["My mom forgot to wake me up","My mom didn't wake me up"]},{"rank":19,"texts":["I didn't know we had homework","Nobody told me","I didn't hear the assignment"]},{"rank":20,"texts":["My cat ate it","The cat ate it"]},{"rank":21,"texts":["It fell in the toilet","It fell in water"]},{"rank":22,"texts":["I spilled something on it","I spilled juice on it","I spilled water on it"]},{"rank":23,"texts":["I was at the doctor","Doctor's appointment","I had a dentist appointment"]},{"rank":24,"texts":["My grandma was visiting","Family came over","We had visitors"]},{"rank":25,"texts":["The power went out","Power outage"]},{"rank":26,"texts":["I couldn't find my textbook","Lost my textbook"]},{"rank":27,"texts":["I did it but forgot to turn it in","I did it, it's in my bag"]},{"rank":28,"texts":["I was grounded","My parents took my phone"]},{"rank":29,"texts":["My tutor didn't show up","My tutor cancelled"]},{"rank":30,"texts":["I was helping my mom","I had chores","I had to babysit"]},{"rank":31,"texts":["My hamster ate it","My pet ate it"]},{"rank":32,"texts":["Aliens took it","Aliens abducted it"]}],"unlisted":[],"source":"No ranked survey of homework excuses exists. Teacher-compiled lists (Jackson Public Schools guide and the standard '100 excuses' lists) consistently lead with: forgot the assignment, didn't understand it, lost/misplaced it, left it at home, dog ate it, was sick, printer broke. 'The dog ate it' is the iconic #1 answer in every published list and in Family Feud-style play.","sourceUrl":"https://ww2.jacksonms.gov/browse/z34Mt5/270002/ExcusesForNotDoingHomework.pdf","reason":"Top 1 kept as the iconic answer: 'the dog ate it' is the first excuse in every published homework-excuse list, even though teachers note it is rarely actually used - this is a 'name the excuse' crowd prompt, so the famous answer is the right #1. Expanded from 5 to 32 using the teacher-compiled lists (forgot, lost, left at home, sick, didn't understand, printer, computer, Wi-Fi, practice, fell asleep). Flag: no ranked survey exists for this prompt, so ranks below #1 are ordered by how often the excuse appears across lists, not by measured frequency."},
